{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105562",
      "title": "Working with Union Types",
      "lectureOrder": 755,
      "videoOrder": 695,
      "sourceHash": "b69d66f1b2cc0092c028db32e1358864168a46cd9046857c931651d022e115bb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "Instructor: Now type inference is great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "And in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "up to this point we already learned quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "about type script and its core types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "But up to this point we also always had the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "that every variable took just one type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 23.31,
          "en": "So we always had just one possible type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.31,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "that could be stored in a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 30.09,
          "en": "Just a number or just a string or just a bullion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.09,
          "end": 33.15,
          "en": "And often that is what you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 37.77,
          "en": "But sometimes you wanna allow multiple different types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.77,
          "end": 39.99,
          "en": "Let's say here for the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "We might be fine with storing a string in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 46.41,
          "en": "but maybe storing a course ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "as a number should also be correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "It really depends on what you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "It's not unrealistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "that we could have a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "where both a string as well as a number should be allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.33,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "Or that you have some variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.7,
          "en": "which should allow two different kinds of objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.7,
          "end": 67.47,
          "en": "And for this scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "that you have more than one type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "which you wanna allow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "you have a feature called union types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "A union type is a type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "that allows more than one type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 82.8,
          "en": "You added like any other type assignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 85.41,
          "en": "by adding a colon after the variable name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "on the left side of the equal sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "and then your type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "Now I mentioned that explicitly setting string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 94.32,
          "en": "again here would be redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.32,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "But it's not redundant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "if you don't wanna use the type inference here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "But if you instead wanna specify such a union type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "Hence, allowing multiple types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "You set up such a union type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 110.46000000000001,
          "en": "by adding a pipe symbol after your first type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "and then adding another type like number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "And you can have as many types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 118.203,
          "en": "which you wanna allow here as needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.34,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "But here I just wanna have string or number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "And now you see that that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "which we had down here before is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 131.22,
          "en": "Because now we are allowing a number alternatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "to a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "And of course, you can use such a union type anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 138.99,
          "en": "where you have a type assignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.99,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "Not just when you're using type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "I could also use a union type up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "Allowing username to be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 150.9,
          "en": "or let's say an array of strings, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 152.79,
          "en": "So that we have first and last name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.79,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "in an array, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "That's also something I could allow here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "Union types are another key TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 166.143,
          "en": "which allows you to define more flexible values and types.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
